window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/resources/soft-v29-107-596f50c912e15bd0.json"]={sha256:"596f50c912e15bd01b40fa8d0f8d91a3da94b04badd8fba737d83e36d868603e",value:{"sources":[{"id":"v29-case-df662c627b7994d4","url":"https://inria.hal.science/inria-00555588","title":"A comprehensive study of Convergent and Commutative Replicated Data Types","titleEn":"A comprehensive study of Convergent and Commutative Replicated Data Types","publisher":"Marc Shapiro et al. / INRIA","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."}],"media":{"courses":[{"courseId":"soft-v29-107","videos":[],"guides":[]}]},"related":{"courses":[{"courseId":"soft-v29-107","related":[{"id":"soft-v29-108","referenceUrls":["https://users.ece.cmu.edu/~adrian/731-sp04/readings/GL-cap.pdf"],"title":"CAP：網路分割時的讀寫契約","titleEn":"CAP: read/write contracts during partitions","why":"用兩課的可觀察驗收條件比較模型邊界：以分量最大值合併離線計數器，驗證交換律、結合律與冪等性。 驗收紀錄必須包含通過/失敗、重現方式和剩餘限制；只對已檢查的模型範圍作結論。","whyEn":"Compare model boundaries using observable acceptance criteria: Merge offline counters by componentwise maxima and verify commutativity,associativity and idempotence. Acceptance includes pass/fail,reproduction instructions and remaining limits; conclusions stay within the checked model.","difference":"透過兩區分割情境說明一致讀取與所有請求成功無法同時承諾。","differenceEn":"Use a two-region partition to expose conflicting promises of consistent reads and universal success.","transfer":"保留單位與邊界條件，僅轉移可證明相容的驗證方法。","transferEn":"Retain units and boundary conditions; transfer only demonstrably compatible verification methods.","practice":["每節點只增加自己的分量；merge=max，總數為分量和；不能用此 G-counter 直接處理減值。 教學基準：max(3,2)+max(0,4)+max(1,1) = 8 A merge B value；第二檢核：max(max(3,2),3)+max(max(0,4),2)+max(max(1,1),5) = 12 all replicas merged value。逐項保留單位、分母、排序或時間界線。 先手算或逐事件枚舉，再使用SQL、試算表或本機腳本重算，保存中間狀態。","CAP 的 availability 是每個對非故障節點的請求都得到回應的形式條件；不是年度 uptime 百分比。 教學基準：1-0 = 1 version gap；第二檢核：2-1 = 1 isolated peer count。逐項保留單位、分母、排序或時間界線。 先手算或逐事件枚舉，再使用SQL、試算表或本機腳本重算，保存中間狀態。","比較兩個模型的輸入、誤差與驗收條件，記錄不能沿用的假設。"],"practiceEn":["Each node increments only its own component; merge=max and value=sum; a G-counter does not directly support decrements. Teaching baseline: max(3,2)+max(0,4)+max(1,1) = 8 A merge B value; second check: max(max(3,2),3)+max(max(0,4),2)+max(max(1,1),5) = 12 all replicas merged value. Retain units,denominators,ordering and time boundaries. Enumerate by hand before using SQL,a spreadsheet or a local script; preserve intermediate states.","CAP availability is a formal condition about requests to nonfailed nodes,not annual uptime percentage. Teaching baseline: 1-0 = 1 version gap; second check: 2-1 = 1 isolated peer count. Retain units,denominators,ordering and time boundaries. Enumerate by hand before using SQL,a spreadsheet or a local script; preserve intermediate states.","Compare inputs, errors, and criteria; document assumptions that cannot be transferred."]},{"id":"soft-v29-117","referenceUrls":["https://nightlies.apache.org/flink/flink-docs-stable/docs/concepts/time/"],"title":"Flink：checkpoint、source offset 與 sink 交易","titleEn":"Flink: checkpoints,source offsets and sink transactions","why":"用兩課的可觀察驗收條件比較模型邊界：以分量最大值合併離線計數器，驗證交換律、結合律與冪等性。 驗收紀錄必須包含通過/失敗、重現方式和剩餘限制；只對已檢查的模型範圍作結論。","whyEn":"Compare model boundaries using observable acceptance criteria: Merge offline counters by componentwise maxima and verify commutativity,associativity and idempotence. Acceptance includes pass/fail,reproduction instructions and remaining limits; conclusions stay within the checked model.","difference":"在 state 與 source position 一致的 checkpoint 恢復，避免兩者錯配。","differenceEn":"Restore state and source position from a consistent checkpoint rather than mixing versions.","transfer":"保留單位與邊界條件，僅轉移可證明相容的驗證方法。","transferEn":"Retain units and boundary conditions; transfer only demonstrably compatible verification methods.","practice":["每節點只增加自己的分量；merge=max，總數為分量和；不能用此 G-counter 直接處理減值。 教學基準：max(3,2)+max(0,4)+max(1,1) = 8 A merge B value；第二檢核：max(max(3,2),3)+max(max(0,4),2)+max(max(1,1),5) = 12 all replicas merged value。逐項保留單位、分母、排序或時間界線。 先手算或逐事件枚舉，再使用SQL、試算表或本機腳本重算，保存中間狀態。","Exactly-once state recovery 需要一致快照及可重播來源；外部 sink 還需相容交易或冪等。 教學基準：2+3+5+7 = 17 recovered final sum；第二檢核：5+5+7 = 17 checkpoint plus replay sum。逐項保留單位、分母、排序或時間界線。 先手算或逐事件枚舉，再使用SQL、試算表或本機腳本重算，保存中間狀態。","比較兩個模型的輸入、誤差與驗收條件，記錄不能沿用的假設。"],"practiceEn":["Each node increments only its own component; merge=max and value=sum; a G-counter does not directly support decrements. Teaching baseline: max(3,2)+max(0,4)+max(1,1) = 8 A merge B value; second check: max(max(3,2),3)+max(max(0,4),2)+max(max(1,1),5) = 12 all replicas merged value. Retain units,denominators,ordering and time boundaries. Enumerate by hand before using SQL,a spreadsheet or a local script; preserve intermediate states.","Exactly-once state recovery requires consistent snapshots and replayable sources; external sinks also need compatible transactions or idempotence. Teaching baseline: 2+3+5+7 = 17 recovered final sum; second check: 5+5+7 = 17 checkpoint plus replay sum. Retain units,denominators,ordering and time boundaries. Enumerate by hand before using SQL,a spreadsheet or a local script; preserve intermediate states.","Compare inputs, errors, and criteria; document assumptions that cannot be transferred."]}],"references":[{"id":"v29-case-3935b8ee3020310a","url":"https://users.ece.cmu.edu/~adrian/731-sp04/readings/GL-cap.pdf","title":"Brewer’s Conjecture and the Feasibility of Consistent, Available, Partition-Tolerant Web Services","titleEn":"Brewer’s Conjecture and the Feasibility of Consistent, Available, Partition-Tolerant Web Services","publisher":"Seth Gilbert and Nancy Lynch","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."},{"id":"v29-case-ce461ff8dfc3d54a","url":"https://nightlies.apache.org/flink/flink-docs-stable/docs/concepts/time/","title":"Flink timely stream processing","titleEn":"Flink timely stream processing","publisher":"Apache Flink","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."}],"overview":"比較相鄰案例與另一組案例的模型、可量測結果及可轉移的驗證方法。","overviewEn":"Compare neighboring and cross-group cases by model, measurable outcome, and transferable verification method."}]},"places":{"courses":[]},"vendors":{"courses":[],"vendors":[]}}};
